  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder so far (0.5203 acc vs 0.4849 for pca_n2000), and image-only is weak (0.2079), confirming RNA as the dominant signal. The multiprofile axis is completely untested. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) with the best-known encoder (scvi_n200) improve over the singleprofile baseline of 0.5203? Why this is the best next step: It isolates the profile-setting effect while holding the encoder at its current best, uses the simpler avgpool aggregation to avoid confounding, and if multiprofile helps, it opens a rich sub-space of configurations (aggregation type, encoder, multimodal fusion) for the remaining 6 experiments. If it does not help, we can confidently focus on encoder (scgpt) or multimodal fusion as the next lever."
}

